2 CONT Åsmund was sent to Copenhagen in 1724 by a complaint to King Frederick Wilhelm de Tonsberg saying Åsmund that 'this bekandte farmer' as a 'uroelig and malicieux Menniske (unruly and malicuous menace). Åsmund was no cowed farmer, b
2 CONC ut rather 'a light and a leader for all other common people' as they said about his father. 'It was a high honor for him, not only for his artistic abilities, but his great skill as a farmer and clearance man, builder,and hunter.
2 CONT
