2 CONT MISCELLANEOUS NOTES
2 CONT
2 CONT served as Vice President and Director of Transcontinental Highways within the U.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Highway Administration
2 CONT
2 CONT some of his photos are included in Photographs of the American West
2 CONT
2 CONT article in Horseless Age Oct 19 1910 "Westgard goes West: pg. 546
2 CONT
2 CONT  Born: Norway - 1859. accord to Library of Congress he was born in 1865
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to US in 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT He began his career as a surveyor doing railroad, municipal, and land work in the
2 CONT
2 CONT Southwest. His jobs included location work for the Atchison, Topeka, and
2 CONT
2 CONT Santa Fe Railroad. From 1892 to 1905, Westgard had been in charge of a
2 CONT
2 CONT corps of engineers working in all the States east of the Rocky Mountains.
2 CONT
2 CONT The corps prepared State, county, and town maps and atlases. His
2 CONT
2 CONT information helped the early bicycle tourists, but proved especially useful
2 CONT
2 CONT when the automobile age began.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Special Agent of the Office of Public Roads at times, and worked for
2 CONT
2 CONT several motoring and road organizations beginning in 1905. In 1912,
2 CONT
2 CONT Westgard Pass in California was named after him (on today's State Route
2 CONT
2 CONT 168 in the Inyo National Forest). The title of an article about Westgard by
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Manchester in the June 1989 issue of Car Collector and Car
2 CONT
2 CONT Classics conveys a sense of his last 15 years: "A Marco Polo of The Motor
2 CONT
2 CONT Age." While on the dedication tour for the National Park-to-Park Highway
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1920, he became ill while passing through Spokane, Washington,
2 CONT
2 CONT traveled by train to Oakland, California, for surgery, but died on April 3,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1921.
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently shot footage for Combitrone Picture Company, distributed by the Pathe Company of a cross country road movie. circa 1916-1917
2 CONT
2 CONT L.E Taylor was the camraman
2 CONT
2 CONT Might be a statue of him at Westgard Pass in CA
