1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Henrik Andreas Pleym'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Rognil Pleym
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Siblings===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16460&idx_id=16460&uid=ny&idx_side=-120 Hanna Elisa Carolina Pleym] - 15 Jul 1792 - Overhalla (parents not confirmed)
2 CONT # [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16460&idx_id=16460&uid=ny&idx_side=-136 Uldrich Christian Jessen Pleym] - 12 Feb 1794 - Overhalla, Nord-Trøndelag, Norway 
2 CONT # [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16460&idx_id=16460&uid=ny&idx_side=-183 Lovisa Mariana Pleym] - 18 Oct 1796 - Overhalla, Nord-Trøndelag, Norway 
2 CONT # [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=16460&idx_id=16460&uid=ny&idx_side=-204 Jacob Edevard Ludwig Pleym] - 17 Jan 1798 - Overhalla, Nord-Trøndelag, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT (Searched birth records from 1780-1807) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrich Andreas Pleym (1796 - 1866) was born in Overhalla (NT) and died in Vadsø. He was a faktor, lensmann (policeman) and kjøpmann (merchant) in Vardo, later Bugøynes. Married to Marianne Sophie Esbensen (1804 - after 1875). The
2 CONC y had 6 children, 4 of which have descendants today. Henrich Andreas is the ancestor of 04.Hovedgren in Pleym-slekten.I Genealogy Book (Schilling, 1930) is not the death year listed. It says that his wife later married Carl Wilhel
2 CONC m Kjelstrup and had children with ham. When I started looking on the internet I found that Henrich Andreas is registered in the census of 1865, when given as pauper in Vadsø. Truly a deep fall! I found that he died in Vadsø 20/12 
2 CONC 1865, and was buried a week later. As a pauper. It said also that he was divorced, a new information that did not occur in Slektsboken.I census of 1865 found his wife in Farsund, wife of the above Carl Wilhelm Kjelstrup and they h
2 CONC ave 3 children. Only the two daughters are known to the author of the Family Book. The oldest daughter was born in 1840. In other words, Henrich Andreas and Marianne divorced before 1840. It was not common at the time? Marianne is
2 CONC  also the census of 1875, now lives in Oslo married to Abel I think the mystery is how one factor, the sheriff and the merchant could end up as a pauper, and why he and his wife were divorced. According to the 1865 Census that all
2 CONC  his children and grandchildren live in the same area (East Finnmark), while he is pauper in a family in Vadsø. The 1875 Census shows that Andreas Henrich grandchildren from his marriage to Marianne lives with her ​​children and g
2 CONC randchildren from her second marriage. Can anyone help me with this mystery?
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: [http://www.geni.com/people/Mariane-Pleym/6000000008620014892 Mariane Sophie Pleym (Esbensen)]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Nicolai Henrik Pleym - 16 MAR 1823 - Vadso
2 CONT >Child of Nicolai Henrik Pleym - [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=9795&idx_id=9795&uid=ny&idx_side=-34 Arent Nicolai Esbensen Pleym] - 19 Aug 1849 - Vadsø
