2 CONT Citing this Record "Michigan Births, 1867-1902," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:NQHK-KN1 : 12 August 2019), Mary Engle in entry for Fred Engle, ; citing , Muskegon, Muskegon, Michigan, 
2 CONC Department of Vital Records, Lansing; FHL microfilm .
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Feb 23 1894):
2 CONT
2 CONT Fred Engle of this city, succeeded in closing a contract yesterday with Captain Loutit of Grand Haven for slating the roof of a handsome new residence to be erected in the Sand Hill City immediately and also for the copper work to
2 CONC  be done on it.  The residence is to be as fine as there is in Western Michigan and will be built of pressed brick and stone.—Muskegon News.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Feb 09 1894):
2 CONT
2 CONT Work will probably commence today on the mantels Fred Engle is to furnish for the Ottawa County court house.  They are to be manufactured in Chicago and will be shipped direct to Grand Haven.  Twelve of them are to be set up and i
2 CONC n working order in 60 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Feb 07 1894):
2 CONT
2 CONT Speaking of the contract to supply mantels to the Ottawa county court houses the Muskegon News says:  “Fred Engle, of this city, was one of the bidders and was the successful one.  The contract price is private.  The mantels will 
2 CONC be of oak and of a very high finish.  Mr. Engle says the court house is much smaller than the court house in this city but that the interior finish costs more than that of the court house here."
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Feb 06 1894):
2 CONT
2 CONT The court house building committee finished their deliberations for this session today.  Fred Engle of Muskegon was given the contract for supplying the new building with mantles.  His bid was $689.  The White Manufacturing Co. of
2 CONC  Chicago were given the contact to put in the new light fixtures.  Their bid was $1100.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Jul 18, 1893):
2 CONT
2 CONT About twenty men are at work on the big court house contract and everything is getting along nicely.  This morning the stone masons began laying the foundation.  All the work is done under the supervision of Contractor A. J. Ward 
2 CONC and he makes things hum.  The cut stone work has been sub-let to John T. Smith of Holland.  Fred Engle of Muskegon has the contract for slating, galvanized iron and tin work.  Most of the brick for the structure will come from the
2 CONC  yards of the Bertschy Brick & Tile Co., of  Spring Lake.  Mr. Ward states that he has not yet let the contract for plumbing and steam fitting.  Of the men at work now, three are from Flint and are stone masons.  James Orr of this
2 CONC  city is keeping time and attending the books of the contractor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Evening News (Grand Haven, MI Jul 1 1893):
2 CONT
2 CONT Fred Engel of Muskegon has been awarded the contract for the slating and copper work on the new court house.
2 CONT
2 CONT (I'm assuming that's a typo)
