1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A complex narrative, it seems to be like this (JM): 
2 CONT
2 CONT FT 1801: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/census/person/pf01058213000957
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Halvor Abrahamsen 17 Oct 1820 https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/gen/vis/327/pv00000001152383
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvor dies 10 May 1830 https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/gen/vis/267/pg00000000962693
2 CONT
2 CONT Moves to Christiania January 1831 https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/gen/vis/291/pu00000000109585
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Fredrik Anton is born 5 March 1831 in Christiania She states that she was married and that the father died before his son's birth.  But this statement is in doubt.  https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/683/120  It seems she ne
2 CONC ver married the father, Samuel Friedrichsen 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Det er ikke umulig at vi står overfor noe kriminelt når vi ser på tidslinjen: Halvor dør, hun blir gravid rett etterpå med sin fetter Samuel og flytter til Oslo for å føde - og tydeligvis for å skjule noe. (JM) 
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrethe probably moves back to Kråkstad with son 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dies 31 Jan 1836 in Krakstad, residence Ascherud https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/gen/vis/267/pg00000000962974
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Fredrik Anton is confirmed 5 Oct 1845 in Krakstad, residence Ascherud  https://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/gen/vis/279/pk00000000328251
2 CONT
2 CONT From Hans Jensen Molbech: "Han ble døpt Hans Anton, men ingen senere kilder bruker mellomnavnet. Navnet Anton går allikevel igjen i slekta senere, så det mulig at han brukte det." lokalhistoriewiki.no ang Hans Jensen Molbech 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Fredriksen: Married 2) 11 Jan 1852.  The bride is listed as 'pige' Margrethe Hansdatter, but it cannot be the same Margrete Hansdatter  since she (partner) died in 1836.  https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/570/660<br/>
2 CONT This bride Margrete Hansdatter married in 1852 was 23 years old, from Lier, and her father's name is Hans Johnsen. 
